Expected elements: present

All backbone items are present: identity bar with a chain-targeting exit (`← demo`, x20-80 y22-40), bidirectional stepping, scrubber, readout, phase rail; Code positioned at line 32; Call Trace/Event Log as one tab strip with Call Trace open; Values as a separate pane below; provenance as the transaction pane's `Data` row. No band above the bar, no spinner, no empty pane, no light chrome. The register reads as the desktop app.

The register damage is in the ink and the copy, not the layout. The amber `Partial` badge (x206-258 y20-42; x1160-1216 y100-122) sits 100px above a reason that says both halves succeeded — P1, and it caps my rating. Below it, a wire enum is dressed in the exact voice of the pane's authored provenance prose (both rgb(162,162,162), same face and size).

Three blue-family hues live in the identity bar alone — link indigo #818cf8, position cyan #67e8f9, accent #60a5fa — and #60a5fa is shared, pixel-identical, between the transient `FETCHING` phase and the permanent `Synthetic demo data` claim. The position cyan has also been lent to the gutter's affirmative arm mark, which appears once per frame, on the current line, with no key.

Fixes: relabel the outcome badge to name the split shape, and rewrite the status reason as English. Then take #60a5fa back from the provenance badge.

Withdrawn on measurement: the cost label's no-break spaces are inert here — `.mddl dd .muted` protects `mana (FeeJuice)`, but the row wraps before it.

Rating: 4/10

